{
  "description": [
    "Swarm references as CIDs, recorded from bee-js 13.2.0 (@ethersphere/core-sdk 0.2.2): Reference#toCid, new Reference(label), and gateway-offer.js's decodeSwarmCid as it was before freedom-core design 0015 SWM-8 PR 8.2 moved it off bee-js (src/main/swarm/swarm-cid.js).",
    "references: each 32-byte reference with its manifest CID (codec 0xfa) and feed CID (0xfb); the decoder gave hex for both.",
    "encodings: what Reference#toCid made of a 32-byte reference in each hex form bee-js takes, and of a 64-byte (encrypted) one, which has no CID form.",
    "invalid: labels the decoder gave null for (expected), with what bee-js's Reference alone made of each (beeJsReference): it decodes some of them to another reference, which is why the decoder checks that the reference encodes back to exactly the label.",
